s types\",\"categories\":[\"Logic & formal methods\",\"Programming language design\",\"Computability & complexity theory\"],\"tags\":[\"curry-howard\",\"lambda calculus\",\"type theory\",\"functional programming\",\"logic\",\"history of computing\"],\"quote\":\"best ~40 minutes I've ever spent.\",\"recommenders\":9,\"score\":10.0},{\"vid\":\"JEYh5WACqEk\",\"title\":\"Why Some Diseases Only Traveled One Direction\",\"channel\":\"CGP Grey\",\"summary\":\"CGP Grey explains why European diseases devastated the Americas while few deadly diseases traveled the other way. He ties it to livestock domestication, dense cities, and the ideas of Guns, Germs and Steel.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a clear, short explanation of one-directional disease spread and the core argument of Guns, Germs, and Steel.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of epidemics\",\"categories\":[\"Medicine & infectious disease\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"domestication\",\"smallpox\",\"guns germs and steel\",\"columbian exchange\",\"zoonotic disease\"],\"quote\":\"I think CGP Grey does a great job at communicating the actual meat of Guns, Germs, and Steel here\",\"recommenders\":11,\"score\":10.0},{\"vid\":\"Ja5Q75hf6QI\",\"title\":\"This Is What Winning Looks Like (Full Length)\",\"channel\":\"VICE\",\"summary\":\"Ben Anderson's VICE documentary shows embedded reporting on Afghan security forces and US Marines in Helmand during the troop drawdown, exposing incompetence, drug abuse and corruption.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended during Afghanistan withdrawal threads as a sobering look at why the transition to local forces was failing.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"afghanistan war\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Military history & warfare\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\"],\"tags\":[\"afghanistan\",\"ben anderson\",\"vice\",\"helmand\",\"war reporting\"],\"quote\":\"I highly 