ies & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"sumer\",\"mesopotamia\",\"cuneiform\",\"ancient history\",\"first cities\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend the _Fall of Civilizations Podcast_ episode 8.\",\"recommenders\":7,\"score\":10.0},{\"vid\":\"dKx1wnXClcI\",\"title\":\"Music Software & Bad Interface Design: Avid’s Sibelius\",\"channel\":\"Tantacrul\",\"summary\":\"Tantacrul dissects the UX and UI of Avid's Sibelius music notation software, going through a long list of bad design choices. The review is both a comic rant and a practical lesson in interface design.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the most entertaining serious critique of a software interface, and a crash course in UX mistakes.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"software ux critique\",\"categories\":[\"UX & UI design\",\"Music theory, synthesis & production\"],\"tags\":[\"ux design\",\"sibelius\",\"music notation\",\"interface design\",\"tantacrul\"],\"quote\":\"might be the most entertaining serious critique of a software user interface ever posted to YouTube.\",\"recommenders\":8,\"score\":10.0},{\"vid\":\"f6kdp27TYZs\",\"title\":\"Google I/O 2012 - Go Concurrency Patterns\",\"channel\":\"Google for Developers\",\"summary\":\"Rob Pike's Google I/O 2012 talk shows how goroutines and channels solve tricky concurrency problems with simple Go code. It features a playful goroutine demo with gophers passing messages and a search engine example.\",\"why_hn\":\"The canonical recommendation for learning Go concurrency, praised as entertaining and clarifying when to use channels versus mutexes.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"go concurrency\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Distributed systems\"],\"tags\":[\"rob pike\",\"goroutines\",\"channels\",\"golang\",\"csp\"],\"quote\":\"Great talk by Rob Pike\",\"recommenders\":9,\"score\":10.0},{\"vid\":\"gNRnrn5DE58\",\"title\":\"Origins of Precision\",\"channel\":\"Ma