ng systems\",\"chaos communication congress\"],\"quote\":\"This is the best description of AGC I have seen so far, from hardware design to mission software, layer by layer\",\"recommenders\":9,\"score\":9.5},{\"vid\":\"yiw6_JakZFc\",\"title\":\"Can YOU Fix Climate Change?\",\"channel\":\"Kurzgesagt – In a Nutshell\",\"summary\":\"Kurzgesagt examines what individuals can do about climate change, covering lesser-known carbon sources and why systemic and political change matter more than personal footprints.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in climate threads to argue that individual action is not enough and that political pressure is needed.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"climate change solutions\",\"categories\":[\"Climate policy, solutions & debate\"],\"tags\":[\"carbon emissions\",\"individual responsibility\",\"systemic change\",\"kurzgesagt\",\"policy\"],\"quote\":\"It's a Kurzgesagt video about why individual action is far from enough, and why we need systemic action.\",\"recommenders\":10,\"score\":9.5},{\"vid\":\"0fKBhvDjuy0\",\"title\":\"Powers of Ten™ (1977)\",\"channel\":\"Eames Office\",\"summary\":\"The Eames Office's 1977 film Powers of Ten starts at a picnic in Chicago and zooms out by a factor of ten every ten seconds to the edge of the universe. It then zooms inward to a proton in a carbon atom.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as the classic visualization for building intuition about scale, and it comes up whenever a thread concerns scale or size comparisons.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"scale of the universe\",\"categories\":[\"Scientific method & science communication\",\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"powers of ten\",\"eames\",\"orders of magnitude\",\"scale\",\"cosmic zoom\"],\"quote\":\"a classic video that demonstrates the scale of the Universe from the micro to the macro perspectives\",\"recommenders\":9,\"score\":