rs and how they generalize familiar tools like cross products and quaternions.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN calls it the best video on geometric algebra, one that makes the subject click in about 40 minutes.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"geometric algebra\",\"categories\":[\"Pure mathematics\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"geometric algebra\",\"multivectors\",\"quaternions\",\"rotations\",\"math visualization\"],\"quote\":\"If you want an inspiring (imho) overview of the power of geometric algebra, I thoroughly enjoyed the video\",\"recommenders\":7,\"score\":9.0},{\"vid\":\"CZIINXhGDcs\",\"title\":\"Debt: The First 5,000 Years | David Graeber | Talks at Google\",\"channel\":\"Talks at Google\",\"summary\":\"David Graeber's Talks at Google presentation on his book Debt: The First 5,000 Years, covering the history of debt, the myth of barter and the Jubilee tradition.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an 80-minute way to get the gist of the book and a different view of what money is.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of debt\",\"categories\":[\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"david graeber\",\"debt\",\"origins of money\",\"barter myth\",\"anthropology\"],\"quote\":\"this excellent talk by the late David Graeber about the history of debt\",\"recommenders\":8,\"score\":9.0},{\"vid\":\"HOuZyOKa91o\",\"title\":\"7 minutes of Pharo Smalltalk for Rubyists\",\"channel\":\"Avdi Grimm\",\"summary\":\"Ruby developer Avdi Grimm gives a seven-minute tour of Pharo Smalltalk's development environment, focusing on tools like search-by-example and the integrated, live coding experience.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a quick, compelling look at what Smalltalk tooling feels like, especially for Ruby programmers.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"smalltalk development environment\",\"categories\":[\"Programming language design\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\",\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\"],\"tags\":[\"pharo\",\"smalltalk\",\"ruby\",\"live coding\",\"repl-driven development\"],\"quote\":\"As a Ruby developer this video about Pharo smalltalk made me a smalltalk believer\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":9.0},{\"vid\":\"LA_DrBwkiJA\",\"title\":\"Compiling C to printable x86, to make an executable research paper\",\"channel\":\"suckerpinch\",\"summary\":\"Tom7 explains how he built a SIGBOVIK 2017 paper made only of printable ASCII bytes that is also a valid DOS executable. He writes a C compiler targeting printable x86 without self-modifying code and solves the puzzles the constraint creates.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN fans call it a favorite engineering video and a showcase of Tom7's masterpiece-level, playful hacking.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"compilers and x86 hacking\",\"categories\":[\"Compilers, interpreters & program analysis\",\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Security & hacking\"],\"tags\":[\"printable x86\",\"c compiler\",\"sigbovik\",\"dos\",\"tom7\",\"machine code\"],\"quote\":\"His video about the printable x86[1] is my favorite engineering video of all time.\",\"recommenders\":8,\"score\":9.0},{\"vid\":\"LJ4W1g-6JiY\",\"title\":\"How close is nuclear fusion power?\",\"channel\":\"Sabine Hossenfelder\",\"summary\":\"Sabine Hossenfelder explains how close nuclear fusion really is to break-even, and why headlines about ITER and lab milestones are misleading. She distinguishes plasma gain (Q plasma) from whole-system gain (Q total) and shows the latter is still far below one.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters post it under nearly every fusion breakthrough story as the standard reality check on Q-factor hype.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"nuclear fusion energy\",\"categories\":[\"Nuclear power & fusion\"],\"tags\":[\"fusion\",\"ITER\",\"q-factor\",\"break-even\",\"energy hype\"],\"quot