 of culture and archetypal characters for the individual, the known and the unknown.\",\"why_hn\":\"Several HN commenters credit the lecture series with helping them through depression or personal collapse and recommend it as long-form learning.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"psychology of belief and myth\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"University lectures & courses\",\"Religion, belief & skepticism\"],\"tags\":[\"jordan peterson\",\"archetypes\",\"maps of meaning\",\"psychology\",\"belief systems\"],\"quote\":\"this series genuinely helped me put myself back together after my ego was shattered\",\"recommenders\":6,\"score\":8.5},{\"vid\":\"LO1mTELoj6o\",\"title\":\"The 7 Habits of Highly Miserable People\",\"channel\":\"CGP Grey\",\"summary\":\"CGP Grey's sarcastic animated video adapted from the book How to Be Miserable, listing habits that reliably make people unhappy. By inverting the advice, it shows what to avoid and prompts reflection on goals and routines.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it widely in advice threads on depression, habits, and goal setting as a funny, memorable way to see what to do by seeing what not to do.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"habits and misery\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"cgp grey\",\"habits\",\"mental health\",\"goal setting\",\"self improvement\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a great video going over the same concepts but in a humorous way.\",\"recommenders\":11,\"score\":8.5},{\"vid\":\"OoJsPvmFixU\",\"title\":\"I Was SCARED To Say This To NASA... (But I said it anyway) - Smarter Every Day 293\",\"channel\":\"SmarterEveryDay\",\"summary\":\"Destin Sandlin of Smarter Every Day gives a talk to an aerospace audience, comparing how Apollo was engineered and managed with NASA's Artemis program. He raises concerns about unresolved details, the number of launches and in