ry Shopping is Better in Amsterdam\",\"channel\":\"Not Just Bikes\",\"summary\":\"A four-minute Not Just Bikes comparison of grocery shopping in Amsterdam versus car-centric North America, arguing that frequent small fresh-food trips beat bulk shopping. It ties this to land use and reduced food waste.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked in urbanism and car-dependence threads as a concise case for walkable fresh-food shopping.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"urbanism and grocery shopping\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\"],\"tags\":[\"netherlands\",\"walkable cities\",\"car dependence\",\"food waste\",\"not just bikes\"],\"quote\":\"had me pretty convinced land use was the key to breaking through a bad food waste vs shelf-stable food trade-off.\",\"recommenders\":7,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"l0GA901oGe4\",\"title\":\"What can Seattle learn from Dutch street design?\",\"channel\":\"UniversityGreenways\",\"summary\":\"Seattle landscape architect Fred Young gives an hour-long visual tour of Dutch cycling infrastructure, covering design details, continuous networks and how cycling fits daily life in the Netherlands.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an in-depth tech talk for urban planning, full of small design touches that make cycling safer.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"dutch cycling infrastructure\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\"],\"tags\":[\"bike lanes\",\"urban planning\",\"netherlands\",\"street design\",\"road safety\"],\"quote\":\"It's a great in depth look for anyone interested in this stuff, basically a tech talk for urban planning.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"l7TONauJGfc\",\"title\":\"NVC Marshall Rosenberg - San Francisco Workshop - FULL ENGLISH SUBTITLES TRANSCRIPTION\",\"channel\":\"Centrum Nadania\",\"summary\":\"A roughly three-hour San Francisco workshop by Marshall Rosenberg on Nonviolent Communication, with full English subtitles added by a fan. He teaches the model with his jackal and giraffe language examples.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters send people to it as the primary source for NVC, recommended for relationships, compassion and difficult conversations.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"nonviolent communication\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Social issues & culture\",\"Productivity & self-improvement\"],\"tags\":[\"nvc\",\"marshall rosenberg\",\"communication\",\"empathy\",\"conflict resolution\"],\"quote\":\"I recommend going directly to the source\",\"recommenders\":6,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"l7rce6IQDWs\",\"title\":\"The world's worst video card?\",\"channel\":\"Ben Eater\",\"summary\":\"Ben Eater explains how VGA signals work and builds a breadboard circuit that produces correct sync timing so a monitor recognizes the signal. He then builds toward displaying an image from simple logic chips.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a clear, from-scratch look at how video hardware works, understandable with just basic logic knowledge.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"building a vga video card\",\"categories\":[\"Electronics & circuit design\",\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\",\"Audio & video engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"vga\",\"breadboard\",\"ttl logic\",\"ben eater\",\"video signals\",\"hardware\"],\"quote\":\"Anyone with a basic understanding of logic circuits has enough background to understand it. Worth a watch.\",\"recommenders\":8,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"nT-TGvYOBpI\",\"title\":\"Cybersecurity as Realpolitik by Dan Geer presented at Black Hat USA 2014\",\"channel\":\"Black Hat\",\"summary\":\"Dan Geer's Black Hat 2014 keynote argues that cybersecurity is a matter of power and policy rather than wishful thinking. He covers surveillance, the vulnerability market, software liability and privacy as the capacity to misrepresent yourself.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited over and over as an important talk, with commenters borrowing its ideas on cheap surveillance, offense-favoring security and liability.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"cybersecurity policy\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\",\"Law, policing & justice\"],\"tags\":[\"dan geer\",\"surveillance\",\"privacy\",\"software liability\",\"vulnerability market\",\"black hat\"],\"quote\":\"Dan Geer, in his incredible talk last year[1]\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"oeYBdghaIjc\",\"title\":\"01 - Course Introduction & Relational Model (CMU Databases Systems / Fall 2019)\",\"channel\":\"CMU Database Group\",\"summary\":\"The first lecture of Andy Pavlo's CMU 15-445 Intro to Database Systems (Fall 2019), covering course introduction and the relational model.\",\"why_hn\":\"Frequently recommended as the best free university course on database internals, praised for depth and Pavlo's presentation.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"database systems\",\"categories\":[\"Databases & storage\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"databases\",\"relational model\",\"cmu\",\"andy pavlo\",\"course\"],\"quote\":\"Highly recommended both for the depth and how Andy Pavlo presents the topic.\",\"recommenders\":6,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"pqzcCfUglws\",\"title\":\"The Psychology of Human Misjudgement - Charlie Munger Full Speech\",\"channel\":\"BuffettMungerWisdom\",\"summary\":\"Audio of Charlie Munger's 1995 Harvard speech on the psychology of human misjudgment, laying out a framework of cognitive biases and mental models for decision making. It covers factors like incentives, social proof and denial.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN regards it as a classic to revisit every few years for improving decisions and self-awareness.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"cognitive biases and decision making\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Investing & personal finance\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\"],\"tags\":[\"charlie munger\",\"mental models\",\"cognitive bias\",\"psychology\",\"investing\"],\"quote\":\"Develop an intuitive understanding of the key mental models mentioned by Charlie Munger in his classic speech\",\"recommenders\":6,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"ras_VYgA77Q\",\"title\":\"DEF CON 26 - Svea, Suggy, Till - Inside the Fake Science Factory\",\"channel\":\"DEFCONConference\",\"summary\":\"A DEF CON 26 talk by investigative journalists and hackers on the fake science industry, with bogus conferences and predatory journals that give studies false credibility. It draws on a large investigation into the money behind them.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a funny but depressing investigation, and the usual link in threads on predatory publishing and fake citations.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"predatory publishing\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Scientific method & science communication\",\"Security & hacking\"],\"tags\":[\"fake science\",\"predatory journals\",\"def con\",\"academic fraud\",\"investigative journalism\"],\"quote\":\"It's a funny talk, if depressing. A great investigation.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"t705r8ICkRw\",\"title\":\"Starbase Tour with Elon Musk [PART 1 // Summer 2021]\",\"channel\":\"Everyday Astronaut\",\"summary\":\"Tim Dodd of Everyday Astronaut tours SpaceX's Starbase with Elon Musk as guide. They cover the high bay, grid fins, Raptor V2, the HLS lander and stage separation, and Musk explains his engineering management process.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as evidence of Musk's hands-on engineering depth and for his advice to question requirements and not optimize things that should not exist.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"spacex starship engineering\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Management, leadership & organizations\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"spacex\",\"starship\",\"elon musk\",\"starbase\",\"engineering management\",\"rocket manufacturing\"],\"quote\":\"Watch this walk around Starbase with Elon and Tim Dodd, and you'll get a pretty good sense that he has an engineering brain\",\"recommenders\":11,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"t_rzYnXEQlE\",\"title\":\"FIXING the ENTIRE SM64 Source Code (INSANE N64 performance)\",\"channel\":\"Kaze Emanuar\",\"summary\":\"Kaze Emanuar explains how he rewrote and optimized the Super Mario 64 source code so it runs far faster on real N64 hardware. He covers performance bottlenecks and fixes in detail for his ROM hacks.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN loves the deep, hands-on look at N64 hardware quirks such as bus contention and the surprisingly large wins from low-hanging optimizations.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"n64 performance optimization\",\"categories\":[\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Speedrunning, glitches & game hacking\"],\"tags\":[\"super mario 64\",\"n64\",\"optimization\",\"romhacking\",\"retro hardware\"],\"quote\":\"amazing video about refactoring Mario 64 to reach 30 FPS and render 6x faster on N64\",\"recommenders\":7,\"score\":8.0},{\"vid\":\"tiJVJ5QRRUE\",\"title\":\"Brainwash: The Gender Equality Paradox\",\"channel\":\"hgoetkehgoetke\",\"summary\":\"An episode of the Norwegian documentary series Brainwash, in which a comedian interviews academics from different sides about gender differences and gender equality. It looks at why more equal societies can still show unequal career choices.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in HN threads on gender gaps in tech as a well-researched look at how gender differences and professional choices may arise.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gender differences\",\"categories\":[\"Social issues & culture\",\