n Rhodes' PyOhio 2014 talk on applying the Clean Architecture in Python. He shows how this high-level design pattern fits Python's features and addresses maintainability problems in large applications.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a practical way to separate business logic from I/O, which reduces mocking and underlies the functional core, imperative shell idea.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"software architecture in python\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\",\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"clean architecture\",\"python\",\"brandon rhodes\",\"functional core\",\"testing\"],\"quote\":\"I'd really recommend this video.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":6.5},{\"vid\":\"DZCBRHOg3PQ\",\"title\":\"Joe Rogan Experience #1258 - Jack Dorsey, Vijaya Gadde & Tim Pool\",\"channel\":\"PowerfulJRE\",\"summary\":\"A three-hour-plus Joe Rogan podcast with Twitter CEO Jack Dorsey, policy lead Vijaya Gadde and journalist Tim Pool. They discuss Twitter's moderation, bans and rule enforcement, with Pool challenging Dorsey and Gadde with examples.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people cite it as insight into how Twitter thought about moderation, and as a source for Tim Pool's arguments about uneven enforcement.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"twitter content moderation\",\"categories\":[\"Free speech, censorship & civil liberties\",\"Tech industry & business models\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"twitter\",\"jack dorsey\",\"tim pool\",\"content moderation\",\"joe rogan\"],\"quote\":\"provided a lot of insight into how Twitter thought about moderation. It was a lot more nuanced than I expected.\",\"recommenders\":6,\"score\":6.5},{\"vid\":\"DleXA5ADG78\",\"title\":\"Brains, Sex, and Machine Learning\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"Geoffrey Hinton's Google Tech Talk linking machine learning to biology, explain